        {
            "description": "Field 'Design Note' differs (PCB: '3V3A rail monitor divider, 1:2 into MCU PA7/ADC_IN7 and (via R37) ADS1119 AIN. FIRMWARE: VA_MON_MV = 2 x ADC. Like the R26/R27 VIN monitor this is a supply health check, so 1% would do; it uses the precision 10k only because R25 shares the position. NOTE the other two users of that stock position, R21 and R22, were deleted with the trim divider and the guard divider, so R24/R25 are now the only ones; revisit the grade at the next sourcing pass', Schematic: '3V3A rail monitor divider, 1:2 into MCU PA7/ADC_IN7. FIRMWARE: VA_MON_MV = 2 x ADC. This IS the sourcing pass the old note asked for. The position was 0.1% 10k (P2TC0603D1002LNTA) only because R21/R22 once shared it, and those went with the trim and guard dividers. Nothing downstream SCALES by this reading -- it is rail health. Contrast VREF_MON, whose ratio main.c promotes into g_cyc.vref_mv and thence into the reported cell current: R34/R35 stay 0.1% for exactly that reason and this pair does not need to. 47k rather than 10k also drops the continuous draw on the analog rail feeding U4/U7/U8 from 165 uA to 35 uA. Source impedance goes 5k -> 23.5k, and that is CHECKED, not assumed: ST DS12232 Table 59 (Maximum ADC RAIN) allows 50k at 12 bits and 160.5 sampling cycles, which is what mcu_adc.c already selects -- 2.1x margin, and more in practice because Table 59 is quoted at a 35 MHz ADC clock where this board runs 16 MHz. DO NOT RAISE THIS DIVIDER FURTHER: 100k legs would put the source at exactly the 50k limit. It releases the matched-pair placement adjacency the two-layer refloorplan work was holding')",
            "items": [
