        {
            "description": "Field 'Design Note' differs (PCB: 'AZ431 bias resistor. (5.0 - 2.5)/1.5k = 1.67 mA nominal; at a -2% rail and the 2.510 V grade limit it is still 1.59 mA, comfortably over the 1.0 mA IKA minimum, and the ~27 uA drawn by the reference node is negligible beside it. Costs 1.67 mA on +5V_ANALOG, which is 17 mV more drop across R32 -- U3 still has ample headroom for 3.3 V out', Schematic: 'AZ431 bias resistor, bought to the 1k stock line R33/R36/R37/R38 already carry. Nominal (5.0 - 2.5)/1k = 2.50 mA. WORST CASE, and the first version of this note got it wrong by using the A-grade 2.510 V limit on a B-grade part: U15 is AZ431*B*N, and DS36721 Rev. 6's ordering table is A = 0.4% (2.490-2.510 V), B = 0.8% (2.480-2.520 V). With the 2.520 V limit plus the datasheet's 10 mV deviation over temperature (2.530 V), R41 at +1% (1.010k) and +5V_ANALOG at 4.900 V: (4.900 - 2.530)/1.010k - 2.530/94k = 2.32 mA. BOTH ENDS CHECKED against DS36721 Rev. 6 Recommended Operating Conditions, IKA 1.0 to 100 mA: 2.32 mA clears the floor by 2.3x where 1.5k cleared it by 1.6x, and is 43x under the ceiling. The change ADDS 0.83 mA to +5V_ANALOG (2.50 against 1.67 nominal), which is 8.3 mV more drop across R32=10R; the AP63205's 4.95 V minimum leaves U3 ample headroom for 3.3 V out')",
